# Hardware Notes

Pin map, validated subsystems and known board issues (rev2 unless noted).
Kept separate from the README so it stays a working reference during bring-up.

Board: custom PCB, ESP32-S3-WROOM-1-N16R8 (16 MB flash, 8 MB PSRAM)
Framework: Arduino via PlatformIO (env: esp32-s3-devkitc-1)

## Build flags required (without these the board boot-loops)
-DBOARD_HAS_PSRAM
-DARDUINO_USB_MODE=1
-DARDUINO_USB_CDC_ON_BOOT=1
-mfix-esp32-psram-cache-issue

## Pin map

### I2C (IMU)
SDA=IO4, SCL=IO5

### IMU (LSM6DSO) — validated working
I2C address 0x6A, WHO_AM_I=0x6C
INT1 on IO2 (not currently used by firmware)

### GPS (MAX-M10S, UART) — validated working
RX=IO15 (ESP32 RX <- GPS TXD), TX=IO16 (ESP32 TX -> GPS RXD), 9600 baud
NMEA RMC/GGA parsed, checksum-validated. No fix indoors — expected.

### SPI bus (shared: display + flash, separate CS)
SCLK=IO14, MOSI=IO13, MISO=IO47

### Display (Sharp LS027B7DH01 MIP)
CS=IO12, EXTCOMIN=IO11, DISP(enable)=IO10

### Flash (W25Q512, 64 MB, 4-byte addressing)
CS=IO9
JEDEC ID validated at boot: MFR=0xEF, TYPE=0x40, CAP=0x20
Read/write/erase self-test runs at boot (FLASH_SELFTEST)

### Buttons (active LOW, INPUT_PULLUP)
BTN_UP=IO8, BTN_DOWN=IO3, BTN_SELECT=IO38

### Power monitoring
PGOOD (USB present, active LOW)=IO21
Battery voltage divider (VBAT/2) on ADC=IO1

### LEDs (active HIGH)
LED_STATUS=IO17, LED_CHARGE=IO18

### Strapping / reset (not user I/O)
BOOT=IO0 (strapping pin), RESET=EN

## Known hardware issues (rev1, fixed in rev2)
- J4 display connector pin order reversed after FPC fold, corrected in rev2.
- USB-C data only worked in one CC orientation — USBLC6 ESD protection was
  not in the D+/D- path for both orientations. Fixed in rev2.
- rev1 had LED_POWER on IO21; rev2 repurposes IO21 as PGOOD (USB-present),
  so anything referencing the old LED_POWER pin assignment is stale.

## Firmware notes relevant to hardware bring-up

- Gyro bias is calibrated at every boot (200-sample average). Board must be
  stationary during the first ~2 seconds after power-up or the bias estimate
  will be wrong for that session.
- `RAW_AXIS_DEBUG` build flag prints raw accel/gyro directly from the driver
  at 5 Hz, before axis remap and before fusion — the fastest way to tell a
  wiring/I2C fault apart from a wrong axis remap or a fusion bug.
- IMU update loop integrates against measured elapsed time (`micros()`), not
  a fixed step, with a 100 ms clamp against runaway stalls. See README for
  why this matters.
